Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/compress.c
Line: 659
Function: bfd_compress_section_contents
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: When using ZSTD, the destination capacity passed to ZSTD_compress is 'compressed_size' which includes the header (new_header_size), but the destination pointer is 'buffer + new_header_size'. The writable region after the pointer is only 'buffer_size - new_header_size'. This overstates the capacity by new_header_size bytes, allowing ZSTD_compress to write past the end of the allocated buffer.

